{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping you during your stay. You're here because you’ve been having trouble swallowing, and we need to do an EGD and colonoscopy. Since you have a lot of medical needs and use a wheelchair, we thought it would be safer to help you with the bowel prep here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. It’s been hard getting the prep done at home. I can swallow liquids okay, but solids feel like they get stuck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll start the prep tonight and do the procedures tomorrow. I also noticed your blood work shows your kidney values are a bit higher than usual—BUN is 97 and creatinine is 1.6. That’s a little concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, is that bad? My last transplant was years ago, but I know my kidneys aren’t perfect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely due to dehydration from the bowel prep and maybe from increasing your Lasix recently for swelling. We’ll give you some IV fluids tonight to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. I have been more swollen in my legs lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. We’ll monitor you closely. Also, your white blood cell count is low at 2.2, so we have to be careful about infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. My doctors say it’s from the immunosuppressants."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2124-06-20 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll keep an eye on it. For now, just rest and start the prep as instructed by the nurse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2124-06-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs this morning show your BUN and creatinine improved—BUN down to 75, creatinine to 1.5. That’s a good sign the fluids helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2124-06-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I also woke up feeling short of breath. I had to sit up to breathe better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2124-06-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I noticed your neck veins were a bit raised, which suggests fluid backing up in your heart. We gave you a dose of IV Lasix this morning, and your breathing should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2124-06-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It already feels a little easier. Is my heart okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2124-06-21 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s acute diastolic heart failure—your heart is stiff and not filling well, likely from fluid overload. We’ll keep you on Lasix and monitor you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The EGD and colonoscopy went well. No bleeding or complications. The colonoscopy was normal except for some diverticulosis and small hemorrhoids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We found esophageal candidiasis—yeast infection in your esophagus. That’s likely why you’ve been having trouble with solids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, like thrush? I’ve had that in my mouth before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very similar. We’ll treat it with fluconazole, an antifungal pill. But it interacts with your tacrolimus, so we need to lower your dose from 4 mg to 3 mg twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that affect my transplant?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re doing this in coordination with your transplant team. Lowering it temporarily while on fluconazole is safe. You’ll need a blood test in a few days to check your levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to go. What about the biopsies?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2124-06-21 13:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The brushings were negative for cancer. The biopsies are still pending, but we don’t suspect anything serious. We’ll follow up with your primary doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2124-06-21 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How’s your breathing and swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2124-06-21 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Breathing is much better. I haven’t tried solid food yet, but my throat feels less scratchy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2124-06-21 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep you on the antifungal for two weeks. Also, we’re adjusting your Lasix. You’ll take 40 mg twice a day for a few more days, then go back to 20 mg twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2124-06-21 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on 40 mg before coming in. Was that too much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2124-06-21 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was appropriate for the swelling, but we had to reduce it briefly because of your kidney values. Now that we’ve corrected the dehydration, we can safely restart the higher dose temporarily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2124-06-21 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat labs are stable. Kidney function is improving, and your breathing is better. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2124-06-21 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Will I need someone to help me at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2124-06-21 20:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You live alone, but you have the emergency response system, which is good. We’ll make sure your prescriptions are ready and your follow-up is scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. We’re finalizing your discharge. Any pain or discomfort?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No pain. My mouth is still a bit sore, but I think that’s from the ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you have some aphthous ulcers. Keep using the mouthwash. Now, for discharge: you’ll take fluconazole for two weeks, continue your regular immunosuppressants—just the lower tacrolimus dose while on the antifungal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Lasix?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take 40 mg twice a day for three more days, then go back to 20 mg twice a day. Your breathing should stay normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. When do I get my blood tested?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transplant team wants your tacrolimus and sirolimus levels checked in five days at their lab. They’ll follow up with the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll write that down. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll have a nurse go over your medications and instructions one more time before you leave. Feel free to ask any last questions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think I’m good. I just want to make sure I don’t miss anything with all my medicines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pharmacy is sending all updated prescriptions to your regular pharmacy. And your PCP will get a summary to help coordinate your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That helps a lot. I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get the discharge papers ready. You should be out by 10 a.m. Take care, and call if anything changes—especially trouble breathing or swallowing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2124-06-22 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2124-06-20 16:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2124-06-22 19:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of kidney and pancreas transplants was admitted for assistance with bowel preparation ahead of an EGD and colonoscopy due to dysphagia and a history of colonic polyps. During admission, she was found to have esophageal candidiasis on EGD, which was treated with fluconazole. Due to a known drug interaction, her tacrolimus dose was temporarily reduced in coordination with the transplant team. She also developed acute kidney injury and acute diastolic heart failure, likely due to dehydration from bowel prep and recent diuretic use, which improved with IV fluids and a dose of IV Lasix. Her Lasix dose was adjusted post-discharge. She remained stable, her symptoms improved, and she was discharged home with follow-up plans for medication monitoring and primary care.",
    "problems": [
      "Candidal esophagitis",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Acute diastolic heart failure",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Pancreas replaced by transplant",
      "Below knee amputation status",
      "Edema",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Peripheral autonomic neuropathy in disorders classified elsewhere",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Wheelchair dependence"
    ]
  }
}
